@pcbeingused333 one regression left in `is-usable-fix.ts`: a fix cut inside an unterminated block comment now passes. `stripComments` (`:178`) only removes closed `/*...*/` pairs, so a dangling `/*` doesn't change the signature and the equality rescue (`:339-345`) lets it through.

Existing `if (a) {\n  run();`, fix `if (a) {\n  run();\n  /* retry the call` → main returns `truncated`, this branch returns `null`. Applied, that comments out the rest of the file.

Flag a `/*` that survives in the fix's stripped text unless the reference has one too, and add the case to `is-usable-fix.spec.ts` (Kody's thread on `:345`).

