**Globs and regexes falsely flagged as unterminated block comments**

A valid fix holding a glob or a glob-matching regex is reported as `truncated`, clearing `improvedCode` in agent-review.stage.ts and raising the bad-fix warning this gate exists to avoid. Require the surviving `/*` to start in a comment position before treating it as an unterminated opener.



<details>
<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>

````text
File libs/code-review/infrastructure/agents/engine/is-usable-fix.ts, lines 339-344:

Globs and regexes falsely flagged as unterminated block comments

`nonLiteral.includes('/*')` treats any surviving `/` followed by `*` as an unterminated block-comment opener, so a valid fix containing a glob — `for f in src/*; do`, `COPY app/* /app/`, `SRC = src/*.c` — or a glob-matching regex literal the stripper does not reach (`p => /src\/*/.test(p)`, which has no `= ( , : return` prefix) is reported as `truncated` as soon as the replaced lines carry no dangling `/*`. `checkFix` then clears `improvedCode` at agent-review.stage.ts:1600 and raises the bad-fix warning, dropping a usable fix — the false-positive class this gate exists to avoid; require the surviving `/*` to start in a comment position (line start or preceded by whitespace) before treating it as an unterminated opener, which keeps both comment tests in the spec passing.

Suggested code:

const opensBlockComment = (text: string) => /(^|\s)\/\*/m.test(text);
if (
    opensBlockComment(nonLiteral) &&
    (reference === undefined ||
        !opensBlockComment(nonLiteralOf(reference)))
) {
    return true;
}
````

</details>


